 "summary": "Gateway profile for the Kohler Decision-Maker 550: 133 objects (76 AI, 29 AO, 28 BI), 59 polled by default. It reads line voltages and currents, frequency, kW, kVAR, kVA and PF per phase, engine oil, coolant, fuel and intake values, ECM status and fault codes, remote start/e-stop/low-coolant inputs and run-time totals. Time delays, voltage/frequency settings and the operating mode are unpolled outputs.",
 "bacnet_transport": [
  "BACnet IP"
 ],
 "firmware": null,
 "default_device_instance": null,
 "access_inferred": true,
 "notes": [
  "Built from Contemporary Controls' BASgatewayLX Modbus device profile Kohler_Dec_Maker_550_Controller_a_LX.csv; the profile maps the registers in the Decision-Maker 550 Modbus register list (https://www.ccontrols.com/support/dp/tp6113.pdf).",
  "Object instances are the ones this profile assigns when it is loaded into the gateway. A site that edited or rebuilt the profile may use different instances.",
  "Only 59 of the 133 rows are flagged for polling in the profile; the rest are served only after you tick them in the gateway. Their descriptions say \"not polled by default\".",
  "The CSV has no read/write column: Analog/Binary Inputs are read-only and Analog/Binary Outputs are commandable (priority array), which is how the gateway maps them (access inferred). Descriptions give the Modbus register each object reads."
 ],
